The wind blows cold today.
My hands are very cold.
I see a large stall with warm clothes.
I walk over to the vendor.
He has many warm things on the table.
I pick up a pair of thick wool gloves.
They are very soft.
"How much do the gloves cost?" I ask.
"They cost two hundred kroner," the vendor answers.
I look at the gloves again.
Two hundred kroner is a high price.
It is too expensive for me.
I put the gloves back on the table.
"No thank you," I say politely.
"Have a good day."
The vendor nods and smiles.
"You too," he says.
I walk on around the market.
